    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0228" n="218" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg218"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-01T16:00:00+08:00">April 1, 1949—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:34 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 185. Allow such clearly calculated accusations re <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chungking</hi> as those contained Peiping 525, March 31 to Department,
                    repeated Nanking 300, Canton 36, go unnoticed would appear most dangerous. It is
                    difficult know how answer effectively, but suggest desirability Ambassador take
                    notice allegation and [answer?] it clearly in hope refutation will reach some
                    ears.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 171, repeated Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
